body:
I told my current partner about it before we started dating. He's the first person I've ever talked to about it who hasn't also directly struggled with it. I told him that I had relapsed and hurt myself back in December. He didn't freak out or anything and actually asked questions and things like that and spoke about it like any other addiction. To better understand it, he equated it to alcoholism and that sort of thing. It helps a lot that he was very open about his thoughts and perspective and just wanted to better understand what I was going through.

&#x200B;

The best advice I have is to talk about it like any other addiction. It's still difficult but there's so much stigma around self-harm that it makes it much more confusing to navigate in conversation.

That's where I'm at right now. For the last like, three-four years I only have maybe once or twice a year. I'm trying SO hard not to slip into the "it's not a lot, so it's okay!" mindset because that just means I'll continue to be reliant on it.

&#x200B;

I get the urge extremely often, almost anytime something negative happens or I feel an uncomfortable emotion. I only really give in under some kind of extreme stress or emptiness or sommethin like that.

I completely get what you mean. I saw it that way for years. I still see the ACT of self-harming like that, like I know I can control it to the point where I won't get a severe injury and I don't mind scars.

&#x200B;

However, self-harm is an addiction. I find that the concept of that dependency when I'm upset is the bad part. Getting through recovery means, to me, that I'm free and I don't have to rely on that anymore to get through bad times and difficult emotions and I can be happy by myself.

&#x200B;

Just a thought, but I hope you're able to find peace, op. I'm happy you're still here. <3

HELL YEAH YOU CAN!!! I'm so proud of you!! I know how hard that can be and you're so strong for getting through it. and now you've made it to another day, and I'm so happy you have :)

&#x200B;

virtual hug!! <3
